## Summary
The article reports that industrial electricity rates in South Korea decrease as the distance from Seoul increases, offering potential discounts of up to 10%. This geographical pricing strategy may impact industrial location decisions and regional economic development.

## Key Points
- Industrial electricity rates are lower farther from Seoul.
- Discounts can be as high as 10% for remote areas.
- This pricing model could incentivize industrial activities outside the capital region.


